// ============================================
// Detection: Endpoint PowerShell Alert
// Source: Microsoft Sentinel Analytics Rule
// ============================================
//
// Description:
// This detection identifies PowerShell-related process execution on the Windows
// endpoint by monitoring Security Event logs for process creation activity.
//
// It is designed to detect potentially suspicious command execution involving
// PowerShell or basic administrative discovery commands.
//
// Trigger Logic:
// - Monitors Windows Security Event logs
// - Looks for Event ID 4688 (process creation)
// - Filters for PowerShell-related process execution
// - Flags command-line activity associated with PowerShell or common admin commands
//
// Why This Matters:
// PowerShell is a legitimate administrative tool, but it is also frequently
// abused by attackers for:
// - Command execution
// - Discovery
// - Persistence
// - Living-off-the-land techniques
//
// Monitoring PowerShell execution provides useful endpoint visibility and helps
// identify suspicious activity beyond authentication logs alone.
//
// Analyst Notes:
// - Review the account that launched the process
// - Examine the command line for suspicious or unexpected usage
// - Determine whether the activity was authorized administrative behavior
// - Correlate with other alerts such as suspicious login activity
// - Investigate for follow-on discovery, execution, or persistence behavior
//
// Expected Outcome:
// This rule generates an alert in Microsoft Sentinel when suspicious
// PowerShell-related process activity is observed on the endpoint.
// The alert is grouped into an incident for analyst investigation.
//
// ============================================
SecurityEvent
| where TimeGenerated >= ago(15m)
| where EventID == 4688
| where NewProcessName has "powershell"
   or CommandLine has "powershell"
   or CommandLine has "whoami"
   or CommandLine has "net user"
   or CommandLine has "Get-LocalUser"
| project TimeGenerated, Computer, Account, NewProcessName, CommandLine
| order by TimeGenerated desc
// ============================================
